00:46:20.945 --> 00:46:23.379
John and James gullick.

462
00:46:25.482 --> 00:46:27.016
I'm sorry to keep you waiting.

463
00:46:27.018 --> 00:46:28.818
The meetings
with the victims' families

464
00:46:28.820 --> 00:46:30.787
have been carrying over
these days.

465
00:46:30.789 --> 00:46:32.789
That's okay.

466
00:46:32.791 --> 00:46:36.225
Allow me to say that most
have been very fruitful.

467
00:46:36.227 --> 00:46:40.563
Agreements are being reached.
Which is why we're here today.

468
00:46:40.565 --> 00:46:43.199
To reach an agreement.

469
00:46:43.201 --> 00:46:46.169
Mr. melnyk, you are the only
family member who has chosen

470
00:46:46.171 --> 00:46:49.572
to sue the company by himself,
without a lawyer and without

471
00:46:49.574 --> 00:46:52.842
signing up with any of
the victims' associations.

472
00:46:52.844 --> 00:46:57.079
I'd like you to know that
you have our complete respect

473
00:46:57.081 --> 00:46:59.549
and that to us it
makes no difference.

474
00:46:59.551 --> 00:47:03.252
Our proposal will
be exactly the same.

475
00:47:04.221 --> 00:47:05.855
James.

476
00:47:05.857 --> 00:47:10.126
Mr. melnyk, this is the
framework agreement

477
00:47:10.128 --> 00:47:12.161
we're proposing to the families.

478
00:47:15.599 --> 00:47:17.133
I would like to just--

479
00:47:17.135 --> 00:47:18.835
it's a friendly agreement

480
00:47:18.837 --> 00:47:20.136
between you and the airline
in which you agree

481
00:47:20.138 --> 00:47:22.872
to withdraw all claims
and lawsuits from the company.

482
00:47:22.874 --> 00:47:25.875
Now, in exchange, the company
will take care of your family's

483
00:47:25.877 --> 00:47:28.845
funeral expenses and any medical
or psychological treatment

484
00:47:28.847 --> 00:47:31.848
that may have been
deemed necessary to date.

485
00:47:31.850 --> 00:47:34.617
The company also agrees to
pay you damages in the amount of

486
00:47:34.619 --> 00:47:40.590
$75,000 for your
daughter's death
and $85,000 for your wife's.

487
00:47:40.592 --> 00:47:45.862
- $160,000 in total.
- I would like to just--

488
00:47:45.864 --> 00:47:47.864
there are also some
minor clauses in the contract.

489
00:47:47.866 --> 00:47:50.867
For example,
you will automatically receive
premium client status

490
00:47:50.869 --> 00:47:52.568
from the airline
within our group.

491
00:47:52.570 --> 00:47:55.271
You'll be able to benefit from
those and other advantages.

492
00:47:55.273 --> 00:47:57.607
These are details
that you should read carefully

493
00:47:57.609 --> 00:48:04.113
because they are clearly
explained in the contract.

494
00:48:04.115 --> 00:48:11.888
I would like for someone
to say that they're sorry
for killing my family.

495
00:48:18.595 --> 00:48:21.197
I want the company to apologize.

496
00:48:21.199 --> 00:48:27.069
Mr. melnyk, let me explain this
to you a little more simply.

497
00:48:27.071 --> 00:48:28.604
If you don't sign this contract,

498
00:48:28.606 --> 00:48:31.674
you're probably not gonna
get a penny for all of this.

499
00:48:31.676 --> 00:48:36.579
Now $160,000 is a lot of money.

500
00:48:36.581 --> 00:48:43.085
Someone in your position
shouldn't turn down
such an offer.

501
00:48:45.088 --> 00:48:47.223
Look at this photo.

502
00:48:49.960 --> 00:48:53.129
Because you didn't before.

503
00:48:53.131 --> 00:48:54.530
Look at it.

504
00:49:02.406 --> 00:49:04.307
Look at it!

505
00:49:19.957 --> 00:49:21.390
<i>Where's your mind right now?</i>

506
00:49:21.392 --> 00:49:23.726
Still feel like you're unable

507
00:49:23.728 --> 00:49:26.262
to engage with your family?

508
00:49:26.264 --> 00:49:28.397
Still feeling pensive?

509
00:49:30.367 --> 00:49:32.335
Well, today let's try to focus

510
00:49:32.337 --> 00:49:36.038
on the positive feelings
you've had this week.

511
00:49:36.040 --> 00:49:40.977
Come... I was really hoping
i could just get a refill
on my prescription.

512
00:49:40.979 --> 00:49:44.680
On those moments
when you feel at ease...

513
00:49:44.682 --> 00:49:48.684
Maybe doing something
you find satisfying.

514
00:49:48.686 --> 00:49:52.254
It may seem silly,
but makes you feel good.

515
00:49:52.256 --> 00:49:54.290
Think about your daily routine.

516
00:49:54.292 --> 00:49:59.395
At home, places you go,
people you see
on a weekly basis.

517
00:49:59.397 --> 00:50:02.164
I really just
want the prescription.

518
00:50:02.166 --> 00:50:07.269
A stroll, a TV program,
talking to a friend.

519
00:50:07.271 --> 00:50:12.742
Look, I don't feel good
strolling or eating,

520
00:50:12.744 --> 00:50:18.547
or seeing anyone,
or talking to anyone.

521
00:50:21.184 --> 00:50:25.221
So just give me
the fucking pills, please.

522
00:50:27.758 --> 00:50:32.094
Or I'll go down the street
and rob the goddamned pharmacy.

523
00:54:28.665 --> 00:54:31.567
"And these will go away
into eternal punishment,

524
00:54:31.569 --> 00:54:35.304
but the righteous
into eternal life."

525
00:54:35.306 --> 00:54:37.539
That eternal life
which Matthew spoke of,

526
00:54:37.541 --> 00:54:42.945
that feeling that tells us our
loved ones are somewhere else,
somewhere better,

527
00:54:42.947 --> 00:54:47.016
is the feeling that must prevail
on a day like today.

528
00:54:47.018 --> 00:54:50.552
One year ago we were
struck by a tragic event.

529
00:54:50.554 --> 00:54:53.656
Many lives were lost unjustly,

530
00:54:53.658 --> 00:54:57.660
incomprehensibly
and unexpectedly.

531
00:54:57.662 --> 00:55:00.963
But today the spirits
of the people we lost

532
00:55:00.965 --> 00:55:03.499
are somewhere else, watching us.

533
00:55:03.501 --> 00:55:10.072
And they can see that on a day
like today we remember them
and pay tribute to them.

534
00:55:10.074 --> 00:55:12.007
And to keep this memory alive,

535
00:55:12.009 --> 00:55:15.010
to keep it ingrained
inside of us,

536
00:55:15.012 --> 00:55:21.317
and in this place, today we
inaugurate this monument,

537
00:55:21.319 --> 00:55:24.753
this memorial to the victims.

538
00:56:12.068 --> 00:56:13.569
Roman melnyk?

539
00:56:15.372 --> 00:56:16.705
I'm Andrew berg.

540
00:56:18.775 --> 00:56:22.511
I lost my wife and my
in-laws in the accident.

541
00:56:22.513 --> 00:56:24.680
I'm very sorry.

542
00:56:26.516 --> 00:56:30.686
I read the story in the papers
about your daughter's necklace.

543
00:56:30.688 --> 00:56:33.055
I thought it was nice
that they used it as

544
00:56:33.057 --> 00:56:35.691
inspiration for the monument.

545
00:56:38.828 --> 00:56:40.429
Do you like it?

546
00:56:41.131 --> 00:56:42.731
Yes.

547
00:56:48.571 --> 00:56:50.773
What do you...

548
00:56:54.110 --> 00:56:57.479
I... I don't know what to do.

549
00:56:59.516 --> 00:57:03.419
I get up in the morning
and I don't know what to do.

550
00:57:03.421 --> 00:57:05.788
Maybe it's not that I don't
know what to do the whole day,

551
00:57:05.790 --> 00:57:09.091
it's that I don't know
what to do in the next hour

552
00:57:09.093 --> 00:57:10.793
or the next minute.

553
00:57:12.762 --> 00:57:15.631
I'm sorry, I'm being so honest.

554
00:57:15.633 --> 00:57:16.932
That's okay.

555
00:57:17.901 --> 00:57:19.601
Go ahead.

556
00:57:21.137 --> 00:57:24.473
Sometimes I try to
think of things to distract me,

557
00:57:24.475 --> 00:57:27.743
you know, just try and think
about something else,

558
00:57:27.745 --> 00:57:31.480
then I immediately forget
and I don't do them.

559
00:57:31.482 --> 00:57:36.652
I just sit at home,
not knowing what to do.

560
00:57:37.821 --> 00:57:39.521
It won't be easy,

561
00:57:40.623 --> 00:57:43.091
but sooner or later

562
00:57:44.160 --> 00:57:46.628
you will find something

563
00:57:46.630 --> 00:57:48.697
that'll help you get out of bed.

564
00:57:50.867 --> 00:57:54.770
- You think so?
- I know so.

565
00:57:55.872 --> 00:57:57.673
Be patient.

566
00:57:58.641 --> 00:58:01.210
That's what I need, dammit.

567
00:58:04.481 --> 00:58:06.515
Have you gotten through it?

568
00:58:13.523 --> 00:58:15.791
- Ever been to Cancun?
- No.

569
00:58:15.793 --> 00:58:18.894
It's a wonderful place
and in the northern tip
of the Yucatan peninsula.

570
00:58:18.896 --> 00:58:22.498
Um, is that something you guys
seem like you're interested in?

571
00:58:22.500 --> 00:58:24.500
- Yeah.
- Yeah, yeah.

572
00:58:24.502 --> 00:58:26.268
Okay, there's a cruise ship
leaving out of Florida

573
00:58:26.270 --> 00:58:27.769
and it heads just
straight down there.

574
00:58:27.771 --> 00:58:29.171
Let me get some
of your information

575
00:58:29.173 --> 00:58:30.806
I'll get you guys started.

576
00:58:58.968 --> 00:59:00.736
How's it going?

577
00:59:01.804 --> 00:59:02.938
Great.

578
00:59:02.940 --> 00:59:05.674
Well, come on, time for a break.

579
00:59:05.676 --> 00:59:07.976
No, I'd like to
finish this side today.

580
00:59:07.978 --> 00:59:10.178
I already opened them, so.

581
00:59:16.219 --> 00:59:17.753
Thanks.

582
00:59:19.722 --> 00:59:23.792
Oh... this week's pay.

583
00:59:23.794 --> 00:59:26.562
Not until I'm finished.

584
00:59:26.564 --> 00:59:30.666
- You're doing a great job.
- Thanks.

585
00:59:30.668 --> 00:59:34.870
If I liked the fence that my
wife picked out it'd be amazing.

586
01:00:19.649 --> 01:00:20.983
Bye, guys.

587
01:00:26.289 --> 01:00:30.025
- Mr. melnyk.
- I need to ask you a favor.

588
01:00:30.027 --> 01:00:32.294
I want you to help me find him.

589
01:00:32.296 --> 01:00:37.633
<i> - Pat, it's Tessa.</i>
<i>- I know it's been a long time.</i>

590
01:00:37.635 --> 01:00:42.137
<i>I'm coming to town, is there</i>
<i>somewhere we could meet?</i>

591
01:00:53.983 --> 01:00:58.754
The book is finished.
I have to send it in
next week for lay-out,

592
01:00:58.756 --> 01:01:02.424
but if you really wanted to say
anything it would be an honor.

593
01:01:02.426 --> 01:01:05.894
That's why I don't wanna
ask you anything specific.

594
01:01:05.896 --> 01:01:09.331
I'm not talking about
an interview or photographs.

595
01:01:09.333 --> 01:01:13.368
I just wanna give you
a chance to say something.

596
01:01:13.370 --> 01:01:16.972
Add a comment, a thought?

597
01:01:16.974 --> 01:01:21.243
Or to not say anything at all,
if that's what you want.

598
01:01:24.747 --> 01:01:29.785
You know, sometimes I...

599
01:01:29.787 --> 01:01:32.954
Sometimes I put
myself in their shoes.

600
01:01:32.956 --> 01:01:35.724
You know, the families'.

601
01:01:35.726 --> 01:01:40.062
And then I think about
my son and my wife,

602
01:01:41.731 --> 01:01:46.401
and it scares me to death,
it's terrifying.

603
01:01:49.706 --> 01:01:51.440
I mean, what can I say?

604
01:01:53.976 --> 01:01:55.477
You know, I...

605
01:01:56.946 --> 01:02:02.951
I just want this pain
inside of me to go away.

606
01:02:04.487 --> 01:02:06.788
So, tell them...

607
01:02:10.026 --> 01:02:12.761
Look, I'm not a bad person.

608
01:02:14.397 --> 01:02:15.797
Right?

609
01:02:34.484 --> 01:02:37.853
- Alright, I'll see you guys.
- See you Monday.

610
01:02:40.790 --> 01:02:44.259
- Have a good weekend, pat.
- You too.

611
01:03:30.039 --> 01:03:33.108
- Yes?
- - <i> I found him.</i>

612
01:03:49.525 --> 01:03:50.992
Hi.

613
01:03:55.498 --> 01:03:58.567
He put his house up for sale
and moved to another state.

614
01:03:58.569 --> 01:04:02.938
He works at a travel agency
four blocks away
from his new apartment.

615
01:04:02.940 --> 01:04:05.273
And what's his address?

616
01:04:07.510 --> 01:04:10.846
I don't know if I should
give you that.

617
01:04:10.848 --> 01:04:12.113
What's wrong?

618
01:04:15.585 --> 01:04:18.620
I'd like you to use this
information in the correct way.

619
01:04:20.056 --> 01:04:24.025
There is no correct way
or incorrect way.

620
01:04:24.027 --> 01:04:26.061
It's not that simple.

621
01:04:29.232 --> 01:04:33.902
I told you, I just want
to look him in the eye.

622
01:04:33.904 --> 01:04:37.873
Show him a photograph
of my family.

623
01:04:37.875 --> 01:04:40.175
I want him to apologize.

624
01:04:41.878 --> 01:04:46.581
No one has said they're sorry.
No one.

625
01:04:58.895 --> 01:05:00.128
Pat dealbert.

626
01:05:02.265 --> 01:05:04.232
Pat dealbert?

627
01:05:04.234 --> 01:05:07.202
His name is pat dealbert now.

628
01:05:11.340 --> 01:05:13.341
Where are you going?

629
01:05:15.077 --> 01:05:16.344
Goodbye.

630
01:06:43.132 --> 01:06:45.000
Is pat dealbert home?

631
01:06:45.002 --> 01:06:48.003
He sure is, that's me.

632
01:06:48.005 --> 01:06:49.704
We're here to
stay the weekend.

633
01:06:49.706 --> 01:06:51.773
I know buddy, I know.

634
01:06:55.444 --> 01:06:57.445
- Hi.
- Hi.

635
01:07:04.120 --> 01:07:06.121
I'm glad you're here.

636
01:07:13.195 --> 01:07:16.031
Okay, let me get your stuff.

637
01:07:16.033 --> 01:07:18.033
We were rehearsing his
lines the whole way here.

638
01:07:18.035 --> 01:07:20.068
Yeah, well, he did a good job.

639
01:07:20.070 --> 01:07:21.469
Hey, you guys are a lot
earlier than I thought.

640
01:07:21.471 --> 01:07:23.705
Yeah, we made great time.

641
01:07:23.707 --> 01:07:26.307
We had a speed demon
in the passenger seat.

642
01:07:26.309 --> 01:07:29.044
I'm just finishing up dinner,
you guys make yourselves
at home.

643
01:07:29.046 --> 01:07:30.145
Yeah.

644
01:07:34.250 --> 01:07:37.218
So who did you
tell him pat dealbert was?

645
01:07:37.220 --> 01:07:40.822
I told him it was
like Clark Kent or Bruce Wayne.

646
01:07:40.824 --> 01:07:43.124
A name you told people
so they wouldn't know

647
01:07:43.126 --> 01:07:46.461
the truth that
you're a superhero.

648
01:07:47.329 --> 01:07:49.364
So I'm... I'm super Jake.

649
01:07:51.768 --> 01:07:53.435
Yeah, at first,
he said it was stupid,

650
01:07:53.437 --> 01:07:57.505
but, then he thought
it was kind of funny.

651
01:07:58.774 --> 01:08:00.308
Yeah.

652
01:08:02.845 --> 01:08:07.248
And, um,
how have you been feeling?

653
01:08:10.086 --> 01:08:11.786
Honestly?

654
01:08:14.090 --> 01:08:15.256
Alone.

655
01:08:15.258 --> 01:08:17.092
Um...

656
01:08:17.094 --> 01:08:20.261
This whole kind of place
feels unnatural.

657
01:08:20.263 --> 01:08:23.131
You know,
i have days that I wake up

658
01:08:23.133 --> 01:08:25.133
and I feel like things
are getting better

659
01:08:25.135 --> 01:08:28.169
and the next day I wake up
it just kind of feels like

660
01:08:28.171 --> 01:08:30.138
things are getting worse.

661
01:08:31.841 --> 01:08:36.811
Well, I'm...
I'm sure it'll take time.

662
01:08:39.882 --> 01:08:41.483
Move here.

663
01:08:44.787 --> 01:08:49.157
Quit your job and move here,
you and Samuel.

664
01:08:50.559 --> 01:08:52.427
Yeah, this'd be a great place
for all of us

665
01:08:52.429 --> 01:08:53.828
to get a fresh start.

666
01:08:57.466 --> 01:08:59.167
And we could all
be super heroes.

667
01:09:10.479 --> 01:09:16.451
I think we just need to...
To take it slow.

668
01:09:16.453 --> 01:09:19.487
You know, I think it's better.

669
01:09:21.390 --> 01:09:25.660
Yeah, yeah, of course.

670
01:09:28.597 --> 01:09:31.533
Um...
I made the bed for you guys

671
01:09:31.535 --> 01:09:34.169
so I'm gonna sleep
on the sofa tonight.

672
01:09:34.171 --> 01:09:35.537
What?

673
01:09:36.572 --> 01:09:39.607
I just thought
that was the plan.

674
01:09:48.284 --> 01:09:54.222
I guess, um, my plan was
we could all

675
01:09:54.224 --> 01:09:57.859
fit in one bed, the three of us.

676
01:09:57.861 --> 01:10:01.829
Okay, well, then my plan
is no longer my plan.

677
01:10:03.432 --> 01:10:04.699
Good.

678
01:12:08.023 --> 01:12:09.090
Jake.

679
01:12:26.342 --> 01:12:27.408
Hello?

680
01:12:50.366 --> 01:12:51.866
<i> I love it.</i>

681
01:12:53.502 --> 01:12:54.802
Mama.

682
01:12:54.804 --> 01:12:56.070
<i> I love it.</i>

683
01:14:07.143 --> 01:14:12.480
I think it all depends on
this card. Oh, wait, no, no.

684
01:14:12.482 --> 01:14:12.480
I win.

685
01:14:12.482 --> 01:14:15.450
- He got us.
- Good job, buddy.

686
01:14:15.452 --> 01:14:16.584
- Alright.
- Let's play again.

687
01:14:16.586 --> 01:14:20.455
- Again?
- Honey, it's late.

688
01:14:20.457 --> 01:14:21.823
Please?

689
01:14:24.460 --> 01:14:26.127
Alright, it'll be a
really quick game, okay?

690
01:14:26.129 --> 01:14:29.464
- Yes.
- I'm gonna fill these up.

691
01:14:29.466 --> 01:14:32.533
You know what? While your
dad's doing that, pajamas.

692
01:14:32.535 --> 01:14:35.703
- Okay.
- Okay, brush some teeth.

693
01:15:05.801 --> 01:15:07.101
Yes?

694
01:15:10.205 --> 01:15:12.173
Can I help you?

695
01:15:12.175 --> 01:15:14.775
Look at this photo.

696
01:15:14.777 --> 01:15:17.545
This is my family!

697
01:15:17.547 --> 01:15:21.782
Listen to me.
You can't be showing up here
like this you hear me?

698
01:15:21.784 --> 01:15:24.218
- Look at it!
- I see it,
but my family's here, okay?

699
01:15:24.220 --> 01:15:26.721
- You killed them!
- I'm gonna call the
police if you don't leave.

700
01:15:26.723 --> 01:15:29.223
- My son is in here!
- No one had apologized!

701
01:15:29.225 --> 01:15:32.693
- You killed them!
- It was an accident, okay?!

702
01:15:32.695 --> 01:15:34.762
You hear me?!
What's the matter with you?!

703
01:15:34.764 --> 01:15:37.698
You can't be
showing up like this.
What have you lost your mind?

704
01:15:37.700 --> 01:15:40.801
I'm gonna call the police
right now, you need to leave!

705
01:15:40.803 --> 01:15:43.804
You understand me?
You need to leave!

706
01:15:43.806 --> 01:15:46.841
It was an accident.
I didn't kill anybody!

707
01:15:46.843 --> 01:15:51.946
What's gotten into you?
You need to leave now!

708
01:15:51.948 --> 01:15:54.749
Have you lost your mind?

709
01:15:54.751 --> 01:15:55.883
You need to leave now
or I'm gonna call the police.

710
01:15:55.885 --> 01:15:58.953
You hear me?
You hear me?

711
01:16:48.737 --> 01:16:50.938
Stay here.

712
01:16:54.610 --> 01:16:57.011
Olena, stay back.

713
01:16:57.013 --> 01:16:58.713
Stay back.

714
01:17:07.289 --> 01:17:08.356
Mommy?

715
01:17:11.026 --> 01:17:12.226
Nadiya.

716
01:17:14.029 --> 01:17:15.796
Don't be afraid.

717
01:17:17.332 --> 01:17:19.367
Don't be afraid, nadiya.

718
01:17:19.369 --> 01:17:20.968
No.

719
01:19:25.427 --> 01:19:27.795
<i> He did not know</i>
<i> that the new life</i>

720
01:19:27.797 --> 01:19:31.031
would not be
given to him for nothing,

721
01:19:31.033 --> 01:19:33.934
that he would have to
pay dearly for it,

722
01:19:33.936 --> 01:19:38.038
that it would cost him great
strife and great suffering.

723
01:19:38.040 --> 01:19:42.777
But that, that is the
beginning of a new story.

724
01:19:42.779 --> 01:19:46.947
The story of
the renewal of a man,

725
01:19:46.949 --> 01:19:50.217
the story of his
gradual regeneration,

726
01:19:50.219 --> 01:19:54.955
of his passing from
one world into another.

727
01:19:54.957 --> 01:19:57.391
Roman, let's go.

728
01:20:15.277 --> 01:20:17.244
<i> So they agreed</i>
<i> to review the sentence</i>

729
01:20:17.246 --> 01:20:20.181
<i>and apply the extenuating</i>
<i>circumstances we presented.</i>

730
01:20:20.183 --> 01:20:22.049
And to be honest, Roman, ah,

731
01:20:22.051 --> 01:20:25.019
I didn't expect them to reduce
the sentence so drastically.

732
01:20:25.021 --> 01:20:28.589
It's been ten years and you
could get parole in four months.

733
01:20:28.591 --> 01:20:30.958
You'll have to visit a
psychiatrist three times a week,

734
01:20:30.960 --> 01:20:33.828
who will write up monthly
reports on your progress.

735
01:20:33.830 --> 01:20:38.866
If you go to every session
and those reports are positive,

736
01:20:38.868 --> 01:20:42.536
you might not have to
go back to prison, Roman.

737
01:23:14.022 --> 01:23:15.322
Hi.

738
01:23:17.092 --> 01:23:18.325
Hi.

739
01:23:22.731 --> 01:23:24.431
Can I help you?

740
01:23:24.433 --> 01:23:29.770
Oh, sorry. I'm, I'm looking
for the exit, I think I'm lost.

741
01:23:29.772 --> 01:23:31.772
It's right over there.

742
01:23:31.774 --> 01:23:35.776
You need to make
a couple of turns.

743
01:23:35.778 --> 01:23:38.078
- Come, I'll take you.
- You sure?

744
01:23:38.080 --> 01:23:40.714
Yeah, I'm heading
that way anyway, come.

745
01:23:40.716 --> 01:23:42.049
Thank you.

746
01:23:52.027 --> 01:23:54.795
Yeah,
I've never been here before.

747
01:23:56.798 --> 01:24:00.734
Oh, last time I was here
was 11 years ago.

748
01:24:00.736 --> 01:24:02.102
Long time.

749
01:24:04.039 --> 01:24:06.740
Everything is
exactly the same.

750
01:24:06.742 --> 01:24:11.045
Nothing has changed since
the first time I came.

751
01:24:11.047 --> 01:24:16.383
The same trees,
the same smell of thyme.

752
01:24:16.385 --> 01:24:21.088
- Same everything.
- No, that isn't thyme.

753
01:24:21.090 --> 01:24:23.524
- It's savory.
- Oh, yeah?

754
01:24:24.459 --> 01:24:27.194
Smells like thyme to me.

755
01:24:27.196 --> 01:24:28.629
But it isn't.

756
01:24:29.798 --> 01:24:32.466
You have family members here?

757
01:24:32.468 --> 01:24:34.234
No.

758
01:24:36.171 --> 01:24:38.639
My father isn't buried here.

759
01:24:47.515 --> 01:24:50.818
You know,
when I was following you,

760
01:24:50.820 --> 01:24:53.153
I didn't know exactly
when to approach you,

761
01:24:53.155 --> 01:24:55.355
where'd be the best place.

762
01:24:56.791 --> 01:25:00.227
But when I saw you
get on that bus this morning

763
01:25:00.229 --> 01:25:03.764
and I realized you were
coming here I thought,

764
01:25:03.766 --> 01:25:06.800
the perfect place
for this to end.

765
01:25:18.780 --> 01:25:20.180
Wait.

766
01:25:21.516 --> 01:25:22.850
Turn around.

767
01:25:26.521 --> 01:25:28.322
Turn around!

768
01:25:45.173 --> 01:25:46.473
Go ahead.

769
01:25:51.546 --> 01:25:53.747
Do what you have to do.

770
01:25:55.316 --> 01:25:56.683
I understand.

771
01:26:05.393 --> 01:26:10.230
But I want you to know that,
I'm sorry.

772
01:26:18.439 --> 01:26:20.807
I'm sorry for what I did.

773
01:26:29.551 --> 01:26:31.385
I could do it.

774
01:26:32.420 --> 01:26:34.454
But I'm not going to.

775
01:26:37.559 --> 01:26:40.294
It's not what I was taught.

776
01:27:07.689 --> 01:27:09.890
Will you just go, please?

777
01:27:17.532 --> 01:27:19.466
Okay.
